{
  "_comment": [
    "Weights for the page score. Data, not code: edit this file to retune.",
    "A page starts at 100. Each issue subtracts its points from its bucket;",
    "each bucket floors at 0 so one bad area cannot sink the whole score.",
    "The page score is the sum of the six buckets.",
    "scope 'page' means the issue is a fault of that page; 'once' means a group",
    "finding attached to one representative page; 'site' means a site-wide",
    "fault that deducts from site_score directly, capped in total, rather than",
    "from whichever page happened to carry the row.",
    "Crawl-layer types have bucket null: they describe the crawl, not a page."
  ],
